      "outputTokens": 1162,
      "costUsd": 0.0105325,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's the graph of three minus t, shaded from zero up to x equals two. Let's give it a meaning. A shopping centre car park opens at nine. For t hours after that, cars arrive faster than they leave, at a net rate of three minus t hundred cars an hour. After noon that rate is negative, so more cars leave than arrive. The shaded signed area is A of x, the integral from zero to x of three minus t, d t. It counts the extra cars, in hundreds, since nine. We use t inside the integral, so that x is free to be the moving end. Think for a moment. When does A grow fastest, and when is the car park fullest?"
    },
