      "inputTokens": 127,
      "outputTokens": 874,
      "costUsd": 0.007929499999999999,
      "pronunciationText": "Let's track A with shapes, like last video. Up to one, the region is a trapezium with heights three and two, so A of one is two and a half. Up to two, it's a trapezium with heights three and one, so A of two is four. Up to three, it's a triangle, so A of three is four and a half. Past three, the graph is below the axis, so new strips subtract. A of four is four, and A of six is back to zero. Plot these points, and A of x makes a smooth curve, like a hill."
    },
