      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 121,
      "outputTokens": 839,
      "costUsd": 0.0076115,
      "pronunciationText": "Now compare the hill with the height of the graph below it. At the start, the height is three, the biggest it gets, and A climbs fastest. At three, the height is zero, and ay is flat, at the top of the hill. That's noon, and the car park is at its fullest, because cars have stopped piling up. After that, the height is negative, and A falls. At x equals one, A has gradient two, and the height there is two. It looks like the gradient of ay equals the height of the graph, at every x."
