      "inputTokens": 113,
      "outputTokens": 807,
      "costUsd": 0.0073195000000000005,
      "pronunciationText": "What if we start counting at ten o'clock, t equals one, instead of nine? Every value of A loses the same piece, the trapezium from zero to one, which is two and a half, the two hundred and fifty cars that came in before ten. So the whole curve slides down by two and a half, and none of its gradients change. At x equals two, the gradient is still one, the height there. A different start gives a different primitive, one that differs by a constant. That's the plus C from primitives."
