      "inputTokens": 135,
      "outputTokens": 1036,
      "costUsd": 0.0093915,
      "pronunciationText": "Now check the earlier results. The trolley's strips settled near two point six six seven. A primitive of x squared is x cubed over three, so the integral from zero to two is eight thirds, minus zero. That's about two point six six seven. The rain gauge's strips settled on one. A primitive of cos x is sine x, and sine of pi over two, minus sine of zero, is exactly one. And the bath's thirty-two litres come from twelve t minus t squared. Ninety-six minus sixty-four is thirty-two. So instead of adding thousands of strips, we need two values of one primitive."
